<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ravi Sher Singh</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">20th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ravi">Ravi</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sher-singh">Sher Singh</a> was the last Raja of Kalsia, a small <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikhism">Sikh</a> princely state in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punjab">Punjab</a> whose lands lay around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chhachhrauli">Chhachhrauli</a> in today's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haryana">Haryana</a>. After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-independence">Indian independence</a> he acceded to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> in 1947, and in 1948 Kalsia was merged into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/patiala-and-east-punjab-states-union">Patiala and East Punjab States Union</a>, ending its separate existence.</p></div>
